  "body": "Part of #3663 (the tool library dialog). Step U8 of the refit to the mockups. It comes first, because the other steps sit inside it.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe tool library opens as a window that floats over the app. The ribbon, the browser and the Properties pane stay around it. Each page has its own buttons in different places. There is no common footer.\n\n## Expected (mockup)\n\n![tool list: mockup left, current right](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/toollib-compare/1-tool-list.png)\n\n- The tool library is one dialog with one header: a \"List\" back button when an editor is open, the tool or holder name, and the tabs **Tools** and **Holders**.\n- One footer for all pages: a hint on the left; **Close** on the list pages; **Duplicate**, **Cancel** and **Apply** on the editor pages. Apply is one undoable command, as today.\n- The content of each page does not change in this step. Steps U9 to U12 change the pages.\n\n## Rules\n\n- crates/ui/AGENTS.md: one component in this PR, its tests, the form seam, frame cost. The `crates/ui` test count does not go down. No snapshot PNG changes.\n- Keep the labels that the existing tests find, or change those tests in this PR.\n- Before and after screenshots in the PR body.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The dialog has the header and the footer of the mockup, and each existing page shows inside it.\n- `layout_window_tool_library` and the structural tests assert the header, the tabs and the footer buttons with their enabled state.\n- Close, Cancel and Apply keep their current commands; Apply stays one undo step.\n\nEffort: high (the frame is shared by all pages and their tests).\n",
